{"skill":{"slug":"1password","displayName":"1password"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1767814883922,"changelog":"Require tmux session for op auth","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2408,"sha256":"5cc0b694c2c26264eff5edc954491bd66cc6b0729f9cdfcdd3d0f9d70d5c93cc","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/cli-examples.md","size":720,"sha256":"7df8fb39623b7cd222766e33255d47c271f772ca53198f256f1270fd9054d20e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/get-started.md","size":994,"sha256":"e5fc5c4fbfd61fa590a2ba903eb7c22bd8d8c622bd47287ff66c20d00d7156b4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2357,"sha256":"51d8bc7258b7e6a057272eb02d959923c58265520e926269466b68162653de4a","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789015055378,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"51c1aba325dcc0f740c1383d90ee2ea4f86a4d47388820d3b86cbd5b9a16a4eb","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/51c1aba325dcc0f740c1383d90ee2ea4f86a4d47388820d3b86cbd5b9a16a4eb","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: 1password\nVersion: 1.0.1\n\nThe skill is designed to integrate with and utilize the 1Password CLI (`op`) for secret management. All instructions and examples, including the complex `tmux` session management in `SKILL.md`, are consistent with the legitimate and secure operation of the `op` CLI within an agent environment. There is no evidence of intentional malicious behavior such as unauthorized data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence, or prompt injection aimed at subverting the agent for harmful purposes. The guardrails explicitly advise against insecure secret handling.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159644656},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":32,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789015055378},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This 1Password CLI skill has a legitimate purpose, but some documented workflows can expose passwords, private keys, or other secrets in terminal output or local files.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Using 1Password secrets is purpose-aligned, but examples such as unmasked printenv, op read of passwords/OTP/private keys, and output files are high-impact secret-handling patterns without enough containment guidance.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The install metadata only declares a Homebrew install of the official 1Password CLI binary and no executable skill scripts were present.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill requires all op commands to run in tmux and documents capture-pane output retrieval, while its referenced examples include commands that print or emit resolved secrets.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact does not install persistent services or backdoors, but it demonstrates writing decrypted secret material such as an SSH key or injected config to working-directory files without permission, cleanup, or git/artifact exclusion safeguards.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill purpose is coherent with 1Password CLI setup and secret use, and access to secrets is expected for this kind of skill.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review carefully before installing. The skill is for a real and sensitive integration, but users should avoid examples that print secrets, disable masking, capture terminal panes after secret commands, or write decrypted secrets into project directories unless they have explicit permissions, restrictive file modes, cleanup, and credential-rotation plans.","findings":"[SQP-2] unexpected: The scanner concern is supported: the reference examples show direct secret output and disk persistence, which are not safely scoped even though 1Password CLI usage itself is expected.\n[E2] unexpected: The op run --no-masking -- printenv DB_PASSWORD example intentionally disables masking and prints a resolved secret, creating a realistic log or transcript exposure risk.\n[E2] unexpected: The env-file printenv example also models printing a secret-bearing environment variable, which is unsafe guidance for an agent-operated workflow.\n[T09] unexpected: The static scan findings are materially supported by artifact text: tmux capture, unmasked secret output, and plaintext output files can expose credentials beyond the intended consumer.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789015055378}}}}}